 "post": {
  "title": "Attackers have started trying PHP2Shell",
  "caption": "Attackers have started trying PHP2Shell. 🚨\n\nThe two critical PHP flaws (CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619) let someone run code on a PHP server without logging in. Security firms report exploit attempts hitting the internet since the patches landed; the UK's NCSC had not confirmed successful attacks yet. The fixes shipped 21–22 Oct: PHP 8.5.12, 8.4.27, 8.3.36 and 8.2.35. Run php -v, and if you're below your branch's fix, update today.\nSend this to whoever runs your website.",
